# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository and check them out as LF on
# every platform. This keeps the JS pipeline byte-identical across macOS/Windows
# (test fixtures like test/sample.srt must stay LF or the SRT parser sees stray
# \r) and keeps the sidecar shell scripts runnable under Git-Bash on Windows
# (CRLF shebang/scripts fail). See context/foundation/windows-port-guide.md §8.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF — Git-Bash chokes on \r in shebangs and line endings.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Known-binary assets — never touch their bytes (most are git-ignored anyway).
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.bin  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.reelproj text eol=lf
